He acts so well.

562
00:21:04,080 --> 00:21:04,750
Let's try another face.

563
00:21:04,750 --> 00:21:05,720
Try a puppy. Try a puppy.

564
00:21:05,720 --> 00:21:06,550
-No.
-Use Jiahao's picture.

565
00:21:06,550 --> 00:21:07,590
-Jiahao's picture. OK.
-Use my picture.

566
00:21:07,590 --> 00:21:08,590
Can it really do that?

567
00:21:08,590 --> 00:21:09,510
Yes. Look.

568
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:11,770
Look.

569
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:13,640
Turn him into a puppy.

570
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:14,480
Let me see. Let me see.

571
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:15,070
How does it do that?

572
00:21:15,070 --> 00:21:15,510
Look, let's...

573
00:21:15,510 --> 00:21:16,200
swap your face.

574
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:17,270
Look, turn you into a puppy. Come here.

575
00:21:17,270 --> 00:21:18,160
A puppy? Let me see. Let me see.

576
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:20,220
It's a dog in your clothes. A dog-man!

577
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:23,110
It turned me into this?

578
00:21:23,110 --> 00:21:23,710
A dog-man.

579
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:26,060
This is actually pretty good.

580
00:21:28,030 --> 00:21:29,160
Where are you going?

581
00:21:29,350 --> 00:21:30,080
Take it easy.

582
00:21:32,270 --> 00:21:33,080
It's fine, it's fine.

583
00:21:33,080 --> 00:21:33,880
Sit, sit, sit.

584
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:34,510
Hey.

585
00:21:34,830 --> 00:21:35,480
It's fine, it's fine.

586
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:36,480
Just as expected.

587
00:21:38,350 --> 00:21:39,850
Good thing we made a backup.

588
00:21:39,850 --> 00:21:41,060
Right. We backed up all the footage.

589
00:21:41,060 --> 00:21:42,260
Fine. Let him take it.

590
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:43,500
The computer was bought
with his money anyway.

591
00:21:43,500 --> 00:21:44,960
So we didn't completely screw him over.

592
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:46,280
He even left us a mouse.

593
00:21:53,190 --> 00:21:54,920
Jiaoqi!

594
00:21:54,940 --> 00:21:55,560
What are you doing?

595
00:21:55,560 --> 00:21:56,720
Run. Run!

596
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:57,920
Why?

597
00:21:58,110 --> 00:21:58,720
Jiaoqi, you have no idea.

598
00:21:58,720 --> 00:21:59,310
What's wrong?

599
00:21:59,310 --> 00:21:59,830
No.

600
00:22:00,020 --> 00:22:02,030
Five or six people
from their village are chasing me.

601
00:22:02,030 --> 00:22:03,270
I took the backroads all the way here

602
00:22:03,270 --> 00:22:04,070
so they didn't catch me. Let's go.

603
00:22:04,070 --> 00:22:05,200
Wait, what did you do?

604
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:05,920
Why are they chasing you?

605
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:06,750
I robbed them.

606
00:22:07,240 --> 00:22:08,640
Wait, their movie
hasn't even come out yet.

607
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:10,070
Aren't you getting
canceled a little early?

608
00:22:10,070 --> 00:22:10,350
No.

609
00:22:10,370 --> 00:22:12,110
I stole the footage they shot.

610
00:22:12,740 --> 00:22:14,140
Why would you steal that?

611
00:22:14,640 --> 00:22:15,590
They got some...

612
00:22:15,590 --> 00:22:16,790
some kind of AI thing.

613
00:22:17,160 --> 00:22:18,350
It can just swap anyone's face.

614
00:22:18,350 --> 00:22:19,400
They wanted to swap my face out.

615
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:21,160
I might not even be
in a single scene anymore.

616
00:22:21,160 --> 00:22:22,480
Let's delete their footage.

617
00:22:22,480 --> 00:22:23,680
Wait, if you delete their footage...

618
00:22:23,680 --> 00:22:25,200
Wouldn't they have a backup?

619
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:26,880
You backed it up, right, Jiahao?

620
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:27,680
Didn't you teach me before?

621
00:22:27,680 --> 00:22:28,640
-Copy it first.
-Yes.

622
00:22:28,640 --> 00:22:29,590
And then paste it.

623
00:22:29,590 --> 00:22:30,650
And put it in there.

624
00:22:30,790 --> 00:22:31,850
I didn't learn how.

625
00:22:35,030 --> 00:22:37,310
You mean we didn't back it up?

626
00:22:41,480 --> 00:22:42,270
It's fine, it's fine.

627
00:22:42,270 --> 00:22:42,960
Even without a backup, we're fine.

628
00:22:42,960 --> 00:22:43,360
Right.

629
00:22:43,390 --> 00:22:45,720
If there's no backup,
we'll just reshoot.

630
00:22:46,510 --> 00:22:48,400
Right. We've been through
worse things than this.

631
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:48,800
Right.

632
00:22:49,550 --> 00:22:50,150
Chase him!

633
00:22:54,330 --> 00:22:56,260
Let me take a look at their footage.

634
00:22:56,870 --> 00:22:58,220
He shot it like this?

635
00:23:00,570 --> 00:23:01,650
W-What the hell?

636
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:05,460
Who are you?

637
00:23:06,510 --> 00:23:07,840
What are you looking at?

638
00:23:10,720 --> 00:23:13,120
What the hell are you doing
with your phone?

639
00:23:14,510 --> 00:23:15,110
I'm talking to you.

640
00:23:15,110 --> 00:23:16,000
Who are you?

641
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:20,020
Someone's talking to you.
Why are you on your phone?

642
00:23:20,880 --> 00:23:21,680
So rude.

643
00:23:26,630 --> 00:23:27,480
Jiaoqi, you...

644
00:23:27,480 --> 00:23:28,750
you're being a little rude.

645
00:23:28,750 --> 00:23:29,200
Emm...

646
00:23:29,920 --> 00:23:33,050
People nowadays
should spend less time on their phones.

647
00:23:42,270 --> 00:23:43,070
It's fine.

648
00:23:43,880 --> 00:23:44,480
It's fine.

649
00:23:45,310 --> 00:23:46,480
How can it be fine?

650
00:23:46,740 --> 00:23:48,740
All the footage is on that computer.

651
00:23:49,030 --> 00:23:50,360
So all that filming was for nothing,

652
00:23:50,360 --> 00:23:51,560
and money was wasted.

653
00:23:51,920 --> 00:23:53,310
Reshoot...

654
00:23:53,310 --> 00:23:54,370
Where is the money?

655
00:23:56,350 --> 00:23:56,880
Hey, Jiahao.

656
00:23:56,880 --> 00:23:57,550
I told you to back it up.

657
00:23:57,550 --> 00:23:58,950
Why didn't you back it up?

658
00:23:59,120 --> 00:24:00,070
If you don't know how to back it up,

659
00:24:00,070 --> 00:24:02,240
you could have just told me,
and I would have done it.

660
00:24:02,240 --> 00:24:04,170
Then this wouldn't have happened.

661
00:24:04,830 --> 00:24:05,430
Well, I...

662
00:24:05,450 --> 00:24:07,650
I thought
he was one of us, so I didn't...

663
00:24:07,670 --> 00:24:08,640
You knew he was a rat.

664
00:24:08,640 --> 00:24:10,070
Why didn't you tell me earlier?

665
00:24:10,070 --> 00:24:10,880
I was afraid your acting
wouldn't be good enough,

666
00:24:10,880 --> 00:24:12,000
and you'd give it away.

667
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:13,590
My acting... I didn't give it away.

668
00:24:13,590 --> 00:24:15,000
But the footage was all stolen.

669
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:16,110
Enough. Let's...

670
00:24:16,110 --> 00:24:17,480
Complaining now is useless.

671
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:18,270
Let's figure out how to solve it.

672
00:24:18,270 --> 00:24:19,510
Just solve the problem.

673
00:24:19,510 --> 00:24:21,110
How about we call the police?

674
00:24:28,170 --> 00:24:30,140
Ma Dajun, what are you doing?

675
00:24:30,880 --> 00:24:32,470
I'm telling you, I, Chen Junnan, am here.

676
00:24:32,470 --> 00:24:32,780
It's okay.

677
00:24:32,780 --> 00:24:33,480
Don't mess around.

678
00:24:33,480 --> 00:24:34,680
It's okay. It's okay.

679
00:24:40,350 --> 00:24:41,030
You...

680
00:24:50,600 --> 00:24:52,280
Is it our computer?

681
00:24:55,050 --> 00:24:55,690
Yes.

682
00:24:55,720 --> 00:24:56,310
It's ours.

683
00:24:56,310 --> 00:24:57,070
Is all the footage still there?

684
00:24:57,070 --> 00:24:58,200
It's ours.

685
00:24:58,240 --> 00:24:58,750
Nothing's been deleted.

686
00:24:58,750 --> 00:25:00,610
It's still here. It's still here.

687
00:25:01,960 --> 00:25:02,950
I got your computer

688
00:25:02,950 --> 00:25:03,980
back for you.

689
00:25:04,110 --> 00:25:05,110
Now we are even.

690
00:25:05,310 --> 00:25:06,110
Even?

691
00:25:06,310 --> 00:25:07,240
What do you mean?

692
00:25:10,510 --> 00:25:12,080
About my mom's ring last time,

693
00:25:12,080 --> 00:25:13,340
sorry for the trouble.

694
00:25:13,470 --> 00:25:15,230
I'm apologizing on her behalf.

695
00:25:20,090 --> 00:25:22,090
The ring incident is in the past.

696
00:25:22,720 --> 00:25:24,580
But now that you've brought it up,

697
00:25:24,640 --> 00:25:26,070
I can finally let it go.

698
00:25:26,880 --> 00:25:28,310
But... but more importantly,

699
00:25:28,310 --> 00:25:30,070
thank you for getting our computer back.

700
00:25:30,070 --> 00:25:30,900
Thank you so much, Big Tough Guy.

701
00:25:30,900 --> 00:25:31,640
You don't know
how important this is to us.

702
00:25:31,640 --> 00:25:32,640
Thank you, Dajun!

703
00:25:32,730 --> 00:25:33,890
-Thank you.
-Thank you, Big Tough Guy.

704
00:25:33,890 --> 00:25:35,480
Dajun, thank you.

705
00:25:36,440 --> 00:25:37,290
Thank you, Dajun.

706
00:25:37,290 --> 00:25:38,690
Stop it, stop it, stop it.

707
00:25:43,080 --> 00:25:44,480
Did you just make a sound?

708
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:46,800
Big Tough Guy.

709
00:25:47,490 --> 00:25:48,290
You can speak.

710
00:25:50,510 --> 00:25:52,430
If you can speak, don't type.

711
00:25:52,750 --> 00:25:53,270
Speak.

712
00:25:57,590 --> 00:25:58,480
I can speak.

713
00:26:03,440 --> 00:26:06,360
It's just that drinking pesticide
ruined my voice.

714
00:26:06,760 --> 00:26:08,290
It's not that I can't speak.

715
00:26:09,320 --> 00:26:10,830
But I'm afraid people will laugh at me,

716
00:26:10,830 --> 00:26:12,720
and then I won't look tough anymore.

717
00:26:12,720 --> 00:26:14,030
You're tough.

718
00:26:14,030 --> 00:26:15,400
You're pretty... pretty tough.

719
00:26:15,400 --> 00:26:16,790
This is our secret.

720
00:26:19,490 --> 00:26:20,550
Don't tell anyone.

721
00:26:23,210 --> 00:26:25,070
Everything's still here, right?

722
00:26:25,150 --> 00:26:26,780
That was close. That was close.

723
00:26:26,780 --> 00:26:27,790
Good, good, good.

724
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:29,220
There are still many good people.

725
00:26:29,220 --> 00:26:31,210
See? I told you.
Prejudice is like a mountain.

726
00:26:31,210 --> 00:26:32,530
Don't judge a book by its cover.

727
00:26:32,530 --> 00:26:33,930
Big Tough Guy is a good guy.

728
00:26:33,930 --> 00:26:35,590
He helped us get the computer.

729
00:26:37,270 --> 00:26:38,930
And that Fei guy is just awful.

730
00:26:39,430 --> 00:26:41,160
He beat Big Tough Guy like this.

731
00:26:41,260 --> 00:26:41,980
Yeah.

732
00:26:42,170 --> 00:26:43,570
His face was all swollen.

733
00:27:00,460 --> 00:27:01,870
J-Jiaoqi, you held up pretty well.

734
00:27:01,870 --> 00:27:03,500
Y-You lasted that long.

735
00:27:04,720 --> 00:27:05,650
I'm getting old.

736
00:27:06,320 --> 00:27:08,050
I couldn't even last one round.

737
00:27:10,110 --> 00:27:12,460
Doesn't my sister beat you like this
all the time?

738
00:27:12,460 --> 00:27:15,660
She never... Well, sometimes...

739
00:27:16,350 --> 00:27:18,000
She doesn't usually beat me up like this

740
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:18,820
Jiaoqi, Jiaoqi,

741
00:27:18,820 --> 00:27:19,640
how about we watch

742
00:27:19,640 --> 00:27:20,830
"Romance of the Three Kingdoms" again?

743
00:27:20,830 --> 00:27:21,550
Take it away, take it away.

744
00:27:21,550 --> 00:27:23,280
I don't want it. I don't want it.

745
00:27:24,070 --> 00:27:26,270
Fei, my head hurts so much.

746
00:27:26,730 --> 00:27:27,660
It hurts so much.

747
00:27:28,450 --> 00:27:29,110
You know what?

748
00:27:29,110 --> 00:27:30,440
He kept pulling my hair,

749
00:27:30,440 --> 00:27:31,350
pulling it back and forth.

750
00:27:31,350 --> 00:27:32,170
It hurts.

751
00:27:32,300 --> 00:27:33,750
Me too.

752
00:27:33,770 --> 00:27:35,240
He stepped on my chest.

753
00:27:35,480 --> 00:27:37,820
I really miss your sister!

754
00:27:38,940 --> 00:27:41,180
I miss my mom.

755
00:27:43,270 --> 00:27:45,190
Jiaoqi, I want to go home.

756
00:27:56,030 --> 00:27:58,300
Tinchiu, our village
is going to be demolished.

757
00:27:58,300 --> 00:27:59,090
Have you heard about it?

758
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:00,010
[The clip is from the movie
"King of Comedy" (1999).]

759
00:28:00,110 --> 00:28:01,350
No matter what you say,

760
00:28:01,350 --> 00:28:03,000
I won't sign it.

761
00:28:03,550 --> 00:28:05,950
No way.
Master Hong offered too much money.

762
00:28:06,160 --> 00:28:07,350
I can't resist it.

763
00:28:07,350 --> 00:28:10,350
As long as you sign,
they'll give you an electric bike.

764
00:28:10,590 --> 00:28:12,050
Even if you talk until the sky falls,

765
00:28:12,050 --> 00:28:14,240
I won't sign it. I won't sign!

766
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:17,730
Isn't this your electric bike?

767
00:28:18,280 --> 00:28:19,200
My son gave me

768
00:28:19,550 --> 00:28:21,030
this electric bike.

769
00:28:23,590 --> 00:28:24,380
He's quite filial.

770
00:28:24,380 --> 00:28:25,440
Where did he buy it?

771
00:28:26,040 --> 00:28:27,790
My son signed the papers.

772
00:28:31,880 --> 00:28:32,480
Tinchiu.

773
00:28:42,590 --> 00:28:43,610
[The clip is from the movie
"King of Comedy" (1999).]

774
00:28:44,400 --> 00:28:45,460
What are you doing?

775
00:28:45,590 --> 00:28:46,520
Are you leaving?

776
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:47,460
I'm going home.

777
00:28:48,790 --> 00:28:49,320
And then?

778
00:28:49,770 --> 00:28:50,770
I'm moving out.

779
00:28:52,310 --> 00:28:53,110
Can't you just not work?

780
00:28:53,110 --> 00:28:55,370
If I don't move, are you gonna support me?

781
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:12,180
What is it now?

782
00:29:16,500 --> 00:29:17,500
I'll support you!

783
00:29:24,910 --> 00:29:26,430
You can support me.

784
00:29:26,450 --> 00:29:28,580
But can you support the whole village?

785
00:29:28,680 --> 00:29:29,550
Such a fool.

786
00:29:31,210 --> 00:29:32,660
Sorry, I'm late.

787
00:29:32,880 --> 00:29:34,200
I wrote it all down.

788
00:29:34,220 --> 00:29:34,680
Here.

789
00:29:39,190 --> 00:29:41,750
Actually, I know you've already signed.

790
00:29:42,690 --> 00:29:43,620
Just take it out.

791
00:30:19,450 --> 00:30:20,300
Shapu—

792
00:30:20,510 --> 00:30:21,780
I'm definitely tearing it down.

793
00:30:21,780 --> 00:30:23,030
No one can save it.

794
00:30:23,750 --> 00:30:24,240
Sorry.

795
00:30:29,830 --> 00:30:30,680
Many people in the village

796
00:30:30,680 --> 00:30:32,440
support your idea of cultural tourism.

797
00:30:32,440 --> 00:30:33,040
Thank you.

798
00:30:34,030 --> 00:30:34,960
You're welcome.

799
00:30:39,090 --> 00:30:41,280
We live in different worlds.

800
00:30:42,050 --> 00:30:44,610
Maybe your world is very dark.

801
00:30:45,720 --> 00:30:46,550
Not really.

802
00:30:46,850 --> 00:30:48,910
It's beautiful once the sun comes up.

803
00:30:51,950 --> 00:30:52,750
Keep it up.

804
00:30:56,920 --> 00:31:00,750
Work hard! Keep fighting!

805
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:03,810
Tomorrow will be better!

806
00:31:16,270 --> 00:31:17,070
What's wrong?

807
00:31:18,790 --> 00:31:19,710
Is it that bad?

808
00:31:21,110 --> 00:31:23,440
The last time I saw
a film with such texture

809
00:31:23,480 --> 00:31:24,570
was "Ma Dasai".

810
00:31:26,480 --> 00:31:27,640
In 1999,

811
00:31:29,270 --> 00:31:30,560
the previous Mr. Chow

812
00:31:30,830 --> 00:31:32,230
came to our Shapu Village

813
00:31:32,470 --> 00:31:33,930
to shoot "King of Comedy",

814
00:31:34,680 --> 00:31:36,880
and my father personally welcomed him.

815
00:31:37,720 --> 00:31:39,240
But due to the typhoon,

816
00:31:39,480 --> 00:31:42,070
he had to set the shooting location

817
00:31:42,230 --> 00:31:43,070
in Hong Kong.

818
00:31:45,350 --> 00:31:47,030
But today, 20 years later,

819
00:31:47,270 --> 00:31:49,800
this Mr. Zhou
has come to Shapu Village again,

820
00:31:50,030 --> 00:31:51,270
and this time, I'm the one welcoming him.

821
00:31:51,270 --> 00:31:52,750
You could say it fulfills

822
00:31:53,200 --> 00:31:54,530
my father's final wish.

823
00:31:54,750 --> 00:31:56,350
On behalf of my sister and me,

824
00:31:56,960 --> 00:31:59,590
and all the villagers of Shapu Village...

825
00:32:03,400 --> 00:32:04,000
Jiahao is getting emotional.

826
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:04,720
Thank you.

827
00:32:05,000 --> 00:32:06,690
-Calm down.
-Thank you, Mr. Zhou.

828
00:32:06,690 --> 00:32:09,160
Actually, I should thank you all.

829
00:32:09,640 --> 00:32:11,920
I'm honored to have worked
with all of you,

830
00:32:11,920 --> 00:32:13,720
and that's how we ended up with this film.

831
00:32:13,720 --> 00:32:15,720
At first, we had no money.

832
00:32:16,160 --> 00:32:18,110
And so many people tried
to mess things up for us.

833
00:32:18,110 --> 00:32:19,830
But we pulled it off in the end.

834
00:32:21,110 --> 00:32:23,550
And look at the numbers from day one.
They're great.

835
00:32:23,550 --> 00:32:25,510
And there are so many
bullet comments praising us.

836
00:32:25,510 --> 00:32:27,440
That shows you made the right call.

837
00:32:27,880 --> 00:32:29,220
Our village is just great.

838
00:32:29,220 --> 00:32:30,970
It will definitely attract
more and more tourists.

839
