Really, try it.

1121
00:40:56,480 --> 00:40:57,890
I-I'm not stressed, mainly.

1122
00:40:57,890 --> 00:40:59,440
If you ever need to bite me,
don't hold back.

1123
00:40:59,440 --> 00:41:01,440
I won't hold back. I won't hold back.

1124
00:41:03,630 --> 00:41:04,550
Well,

1125
00:41:04,880 --> 00:41:06,570
shouldn't your family make some offerings

1126
00:41:06,570 --> 00:41:07,340
and pray?

1127
00:41:07,370 --> 00:41:10,280
Every time we're about to make it,
something goes wrong.

1128
00:41:10,280 --> 00:41:10,880
Now look.

1129
00:41:11,150 --> 00:41:12,880
We're right back to square one.

1130
00:41:16,590 --> 00:41:17,850
Let me tell you a story.

1131
00:41:18,150 --> 00:41:18,760
Go ahead.

1132
00:41:19,030 --> 00:41:20,280
Once there was a village chief

1133
00:41:20,280 --> 00:41:22,210
who led the villagers to dig a well.

1134
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:24,150
They dug 50 meters,

1135
00:41:24,480 --> 00:41:26,110
and there wasn't a single drop of water.

1136
00:41:26,110 --> 00:41:27,630
Everyone was about to give up.

1137
00:41:27,630 --> 00:41:28,800
But this village chief

1138
00:41:28,800 --> 00:41:30,320
stood up against everyone's objections.

1139
00:41:30,320 --> 00:41:32,440
When they reached 52 meters,

1140
00:41:35,880 --> 00:41:37,550
water came gushing out.

1141
00:41:38,230 --> 00:41:38,840
That was amazing, right?

1142
00:41:38,840 --> 00:41:39,230
Yes.

1143
00:41:39,230 --> 00:41:40,630
What does this story tell us?

1144
00:41:40,630 --> 00:41:42,800
The secret to success is often

1145
00:41:44,710 --> 00:41:47,510
just one little push away.

1146
00:41:48,070 --> 00:41:48,800
Understood.

1147
00:41:50,110 --> 00:41:51,510
You've read plenty of "Reader," huh?

1148
00:41:51,510 --> 00:41:52,440
This isn't a story.

1149
00:41:52,440 --> 00:41:53,390
It's a true story.

1150
00:41:53,390 --> 00:41:54,780
That village chief is my father.

1151
00:41:54,780 --> 00:41:56,090
My apologies. Go on.

1152
00:41:56,400 --> 00:41:57,660
So I've made up my mind—

1153
00:41:58,350 --> 00:41:59,750
we'll shoot another one.

1154
00:42:01,250 --> 00:42:02,980
We've already run out of money.

1155
00:42:05,910 --> 00:42:07,910
Don't we still have our acting fees?

1156
00:42:10,230 --> 00:42:11,090
Let them use it.

1157
00:42:11,550 --> 00:42:12,320
Mr. Zhou.

1158
00:42:12,720 --> 00:42:14,520
It's not about money right now.

1159
00:42:14,550 --> 00:42:15,960
It's about copyright.

1160
00:42:16,480 --> 00:42:17,840
We can't shoot

1161
00:42:17,840 --> 00:42:18,960
that IP.

1162
00:42:23,360 --> 00:42:25,160
Don't you guys think it's weird?

1163
00:42:25,720 --> 00:42:26,980
Our film just came out,

1164
00:42:27,150 --> 00:42:29,350
and Stephen Chow saw it from so far away?

1165
00:42:29,440 --> 00:42:31,150
He probably goes online.

1166
00:42:31,150 --> 00:42:33,670
He keeps an eye
on new comedy talent like us.

1167
00:42:34,250 --> 00:42:35,510
What does that tell us?

1168
00:42:35,880 --> 00:42:37,630
Once you're famous, trouble follows.

1169
00:42:37,630 --> 00:42:39,220
We just posted it.

1170
00:42:39,670 --> 00:42:41,400
The lawyer found us so quickly.

1171
00:42:42,800 --> 00:42:45,060
It looks like it was arranged in advance.

1172
00:42:45,590 --> 00:42:47,960
Someone might be playing tricks
behind the scenes.

1173
00:42:47,960 --> 00:42:48,440
Who?

1174
00:42:50,150 --> 00:42:50,810
Gao Jiaoqi.

1175
00:42:53,550 --> 00:42:54,360
Not him.

1176
00:42:54,960 --> 00:42:56,630
If they had this kind
of connection all along,

1177
00:42:56,630 --> 00:42:59,030
why would they have put on
that show before?

1178
00:43:00,110 --> 00:43:01,370
There's someone else?

1179
00:43:02,220 --> 00:43:03,450
Who is it?
